## Status summary
A migration script run against production (instead of staging) truncated core tables in the production database. Restored from the latest automated Azure backup to a fresh instance; data verified and service restored within RTO. ~12h of data lost (within the 24h RPO). Not a security breach — human error, no data exfiltration.

## Response checklist
- ☑ **Leadership assigned** — incident coordinator: Dennis Landfors; recovery lead: Max Netterberg.
- ☑ **Slack thread created in #security.**
- ☑ **Triage & analysis** — customer-facing product down; severity High; no security alerting, so likely an erroneous production change rather than an attack.
- ☑ **Investigation** — a migration script was run against production instead of staging, truncating core tables; confirmed via logs.
- ☑ **Containment** — froze deployments and locked down production access to prevent further writes; preserved the damaged instance for investigation.
- ☑ **Neutralization** — restore the most recent automated Azure backup (~02:00) to a fresh instance.
- ☑ **System recovery** — verify data integrity (record counts, foreign-key checks, smoke test), then cut over; service restored. ~12h of data (02:00 → incident) lost, within the 24h RPO.
- ☐ **Hardening & detection improvements** — add a guardrail to prevent migrations targeting production by mistake (see exercise action items).

